 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "How do you build a mountain out of mud?",
   "exaggeration": 0.7,
   "cfg_weight": 0.45,
   "pause": 0.4,
   "kind": "P"
  },
  {
   "text": "A king of Ur did it around 2100 BC.",
   "exaggeration": 0.5,
   "cfg_weight": 0.5,
   "pause": 0.35,
   "kind": "F"
  },
  {
   "text": "But mud melts in the rain.",
   "exaggeration": 0.7,
   "cfg_weight": 0.45,
   "pause": 0.4,
   "kind": "P"
  },
  {
   "text": "So they wrapped the mud in baked brick, set in tar.",
   "exaggeration": 0.5,
   "cfg_weight": 0.5,
   "pause": 0.35,
   "kind": "F"
  },
  {
   "text": "But water still gets inside.",
   "exaggeration": 0.7,
   "cfg_weight": 0.45,
   "pause": 0.4,
   "kind": "P"
  },
  {
   "text": "So they cut holes through the wall, and laid reed mats between the layers.",
   "exaggeration": 0.5,
   "cfg_weight": 0.5,
   "pause": 0.35,
   "kind": "F"
  },
  {
   "text": "But whose mountain is it?",
   "exaggeration": 0.7,
   "cfg_weight": 0.45,
   "pause": 0.4,
   "kind": "P"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the bricks were stamped with the king's name.",
   "exaggeration": 0.5,
   "cfg_weight": 0.5,
   "pause": 0.35,
   "kind": "F"
  },
  {
   "text": "One now sits in the British Museum, with two dog paw prints on it.",
   "exaggeration": 0.55,
   "cfg_weight": 0.5,
   "pause": 0.5,
   "kind": "L1"
  },
  {
   "text": "That's how you build a mountain out of mud.",
   "exaggeration": 0.65,
   "cfg_weight": 0.4,
   "pause": 0.0,
   "kind": "L2"
  }
 ]
